WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.233
[music]

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.133
[Instructor] We've added our Player
Object to the Scene now,

3
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:12.700
and for this game this entire
platform is going to be

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.500
the center point
of our entire Player View.

5
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.933
We're actually going to
make it so that they can

6
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:19.733
manipulate the View itself.

7
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.300
So we're going to use the
Camera to be able to do so.

8
00:00:23.666 --> 00:00:24.766
How we're going to do that,

9
00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:27.000
is we're going to need
a central point here,

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.366
exactly where the ball is

11
00:00:28.366 --> 00:00:30.333
that we can actually Rotate around,

12
00:00:30.566 --> 00:00:34.700
so we'll Create an empty
GameObject in our Hierarchy.

13
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.700
If we right-click, Create Empty,
we have the GameObject,

14
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.400
now you can see it's spawned
at a strange position.

15
00:00:42.866 --> 00:00:44.866
So we'll fix that just a little bit.

16
00:00:46.066 --> 00:00:49.166
If we go to Transform,
and we click on the icon.

17
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:51.733
We can Reset the Position.

18
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.800
So now our empty GameObject

19
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.800
is exactly in the center
of our scene,

20
00:00:59.266 --> 00:01:01.333
we're going to name
this the "Focal Point."

21
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.700
So in this case, this GameObject
will be the center point

22
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.700
of our entire scene.

23
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.033
It's especially useful
that this is an empty GameObject,

24
00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.433
because this is literally
just going to be a position,

25
00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:16.466
and a point that we rotate around.

26
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.300
In order to control the Camera,
we can actually,

27
00:01:19.966 --> 00:01:22.433
left-click on the Main Camera
in our Hierarchy,

28
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.933
drag and drop it onto the Focal Point
GameObject.

29
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.933
So now the Main Camera is
a child Object

30
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.400
of our Focal Point.

31
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:37.133
And so, in fact,
because the Main Camera

32
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.933
is always tied to the
location of our Focal Point

33
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:43.666
by doing this, if we
rotate our Focal Point,

34
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.366
for example on the Y-axis,

35
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.800
our Camera will actually
rotate around the Game View.

36
00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:55.033
Based on that Focal Point.

37
00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.033
So it creates this really cool effect,

38
00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:00.866
and the center of our platform

39
00:02:00.866 --> 00:02:02.866
is always the center
of our Camera.

40
00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:05.166
So I'm going to reset
that really quick.

41
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:07.866
So now it's back at the center.

42
00:02:07.866 --> 00:02:11.000
Now with that in mind,
what we can do is use code

43
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.966
to actually control the
rotation of this Focal Point.

44
00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.666
So if we go to our Project window,

45
00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:19.033
right-click on Assets,

46
00:02:19.933 --> 00:02:21.966
and we're going to
Create a new Folder.

47
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.066
And this Folder will
hold all of our Scripts.

48
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.233
Now in our Scripts Folder,

49
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:29.233
we're going to right-click on that.

50
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:32.866
We're going to Create
a new script.

51
00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:36.466
And this Script will be
called "RotateCamera."

52
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.733
And this is what we'll use
to control the rotation.

53
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.600
Now we're actually going
to drag RotateCamera

54
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.600
onto the Focal Point,

55
00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.800
so now that the Script
is on our Focal Point,

56
00:02:50.633 --> 00:02:53.933
this is how we can change
the rotation of the Y-axis

57
00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:56.700
so that the Camera always
rotates around that point.

58
00:02:57.533 --> 00:02:59.500
So now it's your turn.

59
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.666
You're going to right-click
on the Hierarchy,

60
00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:04.666
and Create an empty GameObject,

61
00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:08.166
we'll rename that GameObject
to be Focal Point.

62
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.000
You're going to left-click,
and drag your Main Camera

63
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
onto the Focal Point, so that way

64
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.100
it's nested underneath
the Focal Point.

65
00:03:17.466 --> 00:03:20.233
You're going to go into your
Assets Folder, right-click,

66
00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.900
Create a new
Folder for our Scripts.

67
00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.500
And then in our Scripts Folder,

68
00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.700
you're going to Create
a RotateCamera Script.

69
00:03:29.233 --> 00:03:32.366
And then that RotateCamera Script
you'll apply to the Focal Point,

70
00:03:32.366 --> 00:03:36.300
so that way we can give the player 
control of the rotation of that point.

71
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.733
Now it's your turn.

72
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.866
[music]
